  "result": "The NRS_484B_490 rule and its witnesses passed the gate with **OK** on the first run, so 5 of the 6 runs are unused. The gate reported 7 witnesses, 8 names, and no compositions.\n\n**Rule** (`library/TrafficSpec/Rules/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_490.lean`):\n- **Who it covers:** the subject must be a vehicle, written as `ru_aggregate subject \"DEF-NRS-484A-320::vehicle\"`.\n- **When it applies:** the subject occupies some travel region `r`, and some zone sign `d` of kind `narrow_highway` governs `r`, with the sign's legend conditions holding for the subject (`prim_conditions_hold d subject`).\n- **The duty:** `¬ drv_motion_parked subject [p.halt_speed_tolerance, p.parking_min_duration]`.\n- **Choices:** I added no narrowings. I also left out a \"not an end-of-zone sign\" condition, because the node doesn't state one and the trigger span (d1) may not be narrowed.\n\n**Witnesses** (`library/TrafficSpecWitness/NRS_484B/NRS_484B_490.lean`): two side-by-side lanes and one zone sign, with an observation every 10 s. Each scenario is judged only at instants whose full 180 s look-back lies inside the recording, so no instant comes out unknown because the window runs past the start.\n\n| Scenario | Expected | What happens |\n|---|---|---|\n| forbid | violated | The vehicle stands for 220 s; judged at 200–240 s |\n| permit | compliant | The vehicle halts 20 s and drives on; judged at 200–290 s |\n| idle | not applicable | The narrow-highway sign governs the other lane |\n| blind | unknown | Which regions the sign governs is unobserved (`dev.governs` masked) |\n| branch_1 | not applicable | The sign is of kind `parking_restricted` |\n| branch_2 | not applicable | The sign applies Mon–Fri 07:00–09:00, and it is Saturday noon |\n| branch_3 | not applicable | The subject is a pedestrian, not a vehicle |\n\nThe three `branch_*` witnesses are extra. I added them so that the sign kind, the conditions check and the vehicle class each decide at least one witness.\n\n`task_result.md` is written in the working directory.",
